  "notes": "West leads the ♠J against 4♥. When East wins his ♠A and switches to a club, right into dummy's powerful holding, South should worry about East having been dealt a singleton club.\n\nSouth is in danger of losing tricks to the ♥K and ♦K in addition to the ♠A. South can afford to lose those 3 tricks, but he cannot afford to have West give East a club ruff as well.\n\nSouth should cash the ♥A and concede a heart trick to the ♥K. East wins the ♥K and returns a diamond. East has a trump left, making the diamond finesse too dangerous. Should that finesse lose to the ♦K in West, a club ruff will defeat the contract.\n\nTaking an early heart finesse would be wrong as well. If West was dealt the ♥K, East may get a club ruff, leaving the fate of the contract dependent on the diamond finesse.",
